@model HomeViewModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Student budgeting made simple"; }
<form id="security-token" class="visually-hidden">@Html.AntiForgeryToken()</form>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-orb hero-orb-one"></div><div class="hero-orb hero-orb-two"></div>
    <div class="container hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Money confidence starts here</span><h1>Make every rupee<br /><em>work smarter.</em></h1><p>Simple lessons and practical tools designed for students who want less money stress and stronger everyday habits.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="#tools">Build my budget</a><a class="text-link" href="#learn">Explore the basics <span>→</span></a></div><div class="trust-row"><span>✓ No bank details</span><span>✓ Private planning</span><span>✓ Beginner friendly</span></div></div>
        <div class="hero-visual reveal"><div class="budget-card" data-tilt><div class="budget-card-head"><div><small>MONTHLY PLAN</small><strong>Smart split</strong></div><span class="mini-logo">B</span></div><div class="donut" aria-label="Example budget: 50 percent needs, 30 percent wants, 20 percent savings"><span>100%<small>planned</small></span></div><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot needs"></i>Needs <b>50%</b></span><span><i class="dot wants"></i>Wants <b>30%</b></span><span><i class="dot savings"></i>Savings <b>20%</b></span></div></div><div class="floating-note note-one">↗ <strong>Save first</strong><small>Build the habit</small></div><div class="floating-note note-two">★ <strong>Student-ready</strong><small>Made for real life</small></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container quick-strip"><span><strong data-counter="@Model.VisitCount">@Model.VisitCount.ToString("N0")</strong> learning visits</span><span id="live-clock">Loading local time…</span><span><strong data-counter="7">7</strong> practical tools & guides</span></div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="learn"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with the essentials</span><h2>Budgeting without the jargon</h2></div><p>Understand where money comes from, where it goes, and how to stay in control.</p></div>
    <div class="concept-grid searchable-content">
        <article class="concept-card" data-topic="income basics"><span class="concept-icon mint">↙</span><h3>Income</h3><p>Money from an allowance, scholarship, job, freelance work, or family support.</p><small>Example: PKR 30,000 internship income</small></article>
        <article class="concept-card" data-topic="fixed expenses basics"><span class="concept-icon blue">▣</span><h3>Fixed expenses</h3><p>Regular costs that usually stay similar, such as fees, rent, or a subscription.</p><small>Plan these first</small></article>
        <article class="concept-card" data-topic="variable expenses basics"><span class="concept-icon orange">↝</span><h3>Variable expenses</h3><p>Costs that change, including food, transport, entertainment, and shopping.</p><small>Track these weekly</small></article>
        <article class="concept-card" data-topic="savings goals basics"><span class="concept-icon purple">◒</span><h3>Savings</h3><p>Money set aside for emergencies, future goals, or planned purchases.</p><small>Small amounts still count</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="sample-budget panel searchable-content" data-topic="budget income expenses savings"><div><span class="eyebrow">Example</span><h3>A student's PKR 30,000 monthly plan</h3><p>These values are samples—not a prescription.</p></div><div class="budget-rows"><span><i class="bar needs" style="width:50%"></i><b>Needs</b><strong>PKR 15,000</strong></span><span><i class="bar wants" style="width:30%"></i><b>Wants</b><strong>PKR 9,000</strong></span><span><i class="bar savings" style="width:20%"></i><b>Savings</b><strong>PKR 6,000</strong></span></div></div>
    <div class="needs-panel panel" id="needs-wants"><div><span class="eyebrow">Quick knowledge check</span><h3>Need or want?</h3><p id="quiz-question">A textbook is required for tomorrow's class. Is it a need or a want?</p><div class="needs-examples" aria-label="Needs and wants examples"><div><b>Essential needs</b><span>Basic meals</span><span>Required course material</span><span>Safe transport</span><span>Medicine and housing</span></div><div><b>Optional wants</b><span>Premium takeaway</span><span>Fashion upgrades</span><span>Entertainment subscriptions</span><span>Latest gadgets</span></div></div></div><div class="quiz-actions"><span id="quiz-progress" class="quiz-progress">Question 1 of 6</span><button class="btn btn-choice" type="button" data-answer="need">Essential need</button><button class="btn btn-choice" type="button" data-answer="want">Optional want</button><p id="quiz-feedback" class="quiz-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><button id="next-quiz" class="btn btn-soft" type="button" hidden>Next question →</button></div><div class="decision-guide"><b>Pause before buying:</b><span>Do I need it now?</span><span>Can I afford it?</span><span>Will I still want it tomorrow?</span></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section section-tint" id="tools"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Try it yourself</span><h2>Practical planning tools</h2></div><p>Calculator values stay temporary. Expense rows are saved only when you choose to use a signed-in account.</p></div>
    <div class="tools-grid">
        <article class="tool-card"><div class="tool-title"><span>01</span><div><h3>50-30-20 calculator</h3><p>See a suggested learning split for any sample income.</p></div></div><form id="budget-form" novalidate><label for="monthly-income">Monthly income</label><div class="money-input"><span>PKR</span><input id="monthly-income" name="MonthlyIncome" type="number" min="1" max="1000000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="30,000" required /></div><button class="btn btn-primary w-100" type="submit">Calculate my split</button></form><div id="budget-result" class="tool-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div><small class="disclaimer">Educational guideline only. Adjust the percentages to your circumstances.</small></article>
        <article class="tool-card"><div class="tool-title"><span>02</span><div><h3>Savings goal</h3><p>Estimate the time needed to reach a meaningful goal.</p></div></div><form id="goal-form" novalidate><label for="goal-name">Goal name</label><input id="goal-name" name="GoalName" maxlength="80" placeholder="New laptop" required /><div class="form-pair"><div><label for="target-amount">Target</label><input id="target-amount" name="TargetAmount" type="number" min="1" max="1000000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="120000" required /></div><div><label for="current-savings">Saved</label><input id="current-savings" name="CurrentSavings" type="number" min="0" max="1000000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="20000" required /></div></div><label for="monthly-contribution">Monthly contribution</label><input id="monthly-contribution" name="MonthlyContribution" type="number" min="1" max="1000000000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="10000" required /><button class="btn btn-primary w-100" type="submit">Estimate my goal</button></form><div id="goal-result" class="tool-result" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div></article>
    </div>
    <article class="planner panel" data-persistent="@(User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true ? "true" : "false")"><div class="planner-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">@(User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true ? "Secure account planner" : "Current-session demo")</span><h3>Expense planner</h3><p>@if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true) { <text>Add, edit, and remove expenses saved securely to your account.</text> } else { <text>Your sample rows stay in this tab only. <a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login">Log in</a> to save them.</text> }</p><p id="expense-status" class="planner-status" role="status"></p></div><div><label for="planner-balance">Monthly balance</label><input id="planner-balance" type="number" min="0" value="30000" /></div></div><form id="expense-form" class="expense-form"><input id="expense-id" name="Id" type="hidden" /><label>Date<input id="expense-date" name="Date" type="date" required /></label><label>Category<select id="expense-category" name="Category"><option>Food</option><option>Transport</option><option>Education</option><option>Entertainment</option><option>Shopping</option><option>Utilities</option><option>Miscellaneous</option></select></label><label>Description<input id="expense-description" name="Description" maxlength="80" placeholder="Bus pass" required /></label><label>Amount<input id="expense-amount" name="Amount" type="number" min="0.01" step="0.01" required /></label><button class="btn btn-dark" type="submit">Save expense</button></form><div class="table-responsive"><table class="expense-table"><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Category</th><th>Description</th><th>Amount</th><th><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></th></tr></thead><tbody id="expense-list"><tr class="empty-row"><td colspan="5">No expenses yet.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="planner-summary"><span>Planned expenses <strong id="expense-total">PKR 0</strong></span><span>Remaining balance <strong id="remaining-balance">PKR 30,000</strong></span></div></article>
</div></section>

<section class="section" id="mistakes"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Spot the pattern</span><h2>Common money mistakes</h2></div><p>Realistic student situations—and one useful correction for each.</p></div><div class="mistake-grid searchable-content">
    <details data-topic="mistakes impulse shopping"><summary><span>🛍</span><div><h3>Impulse buying</h3><p>“It was on sale, so I bought it.”</p></div></summary><p><b>Try this:</b> Wait 24 hours and check whether it fits your wants budget.</p></details>
    <details data-topic="mistakes small expenses food"><summary><span>☕</span><div><h3>Ignoring small expenses</h3><p>Daily snacks quietly add up.</p></div></summary><p><b>Try this:</b> Track small purchases for seven days before setting a weekly limit.</p></details>
    <details data-topic="mistakes subscriptions"><summary><span>↻</span><div><h3>Unused subscriptions</h3><p>Paying for services you forgot.</p></div></summary><p><b>Try this:</b> Review recurring charges once a month and cancel unused plans.</p></details>
    <details data-topic="mistakes late payments fees"><summary><span>⏱</span><div><h3>Late payments</h3><p>A missed due date creates avoidable fees.</p></div></summary><p><b>Try this:</b> Put due dates in your calendar and set a reminder several days early.</p></details>
    <details data-topic="mistakes plan late payments"><summary><span>!</span><div><h3>Spending without a plan</h3><p>Essentials are left until last.</p></div></summary><p><b>Try this:</b> Separate needs and savings as soon as income arrives.</p></details>
</div></div></section>

<section class="section section-tint" id="smart-tips"><div class="container smart-tip-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Database-powered guidance</span><h2>Get a tip for your spending habit</h2><p>Choose the area you want to improve. BudgetBasics selects a practical student tip from its preloaded learning library.</p><div class="tip-controls"><label for="habit-tip-select">Spending habit</label><select id="habit-tip-select"><option value="all">General money habits</option><option value="food">Food and takeaway</option><option value="transport">Transport</option><option value="impulse">Impulse shopping</option><option value="subscriptions">Subscriptions</option><option value="saving">Saving regularly</option></select><button id="habit-tip-button" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Show my tip</button></div></div><article id="habit-tip-result" class="smart-tip-card" aria-live="polite"><span class="tip-spark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><small>SMART STUDENT TIP</small><h3>Choose a habit to begin</h3><p>Your tip will appear here. The advice is educational and does not use bank or card information.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="section section-dark" id="resources"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading light"><div><span class="eyebrow">Visual learning gallery</span><h2>See the bigger picture</h2></div><div class="search-box"><label class="visually-hidden" for="content-search">Search learning content</label><input id="content-search" type="search" placeholder="Search saving, needs, goals…" /><label class="visually-hidden" for="content-sort">Sort gallery</label><select id="content-sort"><option value="default">Featured first</option><option value="az">A–Z</option></select></div></div><div class="filter-row" role="group" aria-label="Filter gallery"><button class="active" data-filter="all">All topics</button><button data-filter="budget">Budgeting</button><button data-filter="saving">Saving</button><button data-filter="needs">Needs & wants</button></div><div class="gallery searchable-content">
    <figure data-topic="budget 50 30 20"><div class="graphic split-graphic"><span>50<small>Needs</small></span><span>30<small>Wants</small></span><span>20<small>Save</small></span></div><figcaption><b>The balanced split</b><span>A flexible starting point for planning.</span></figcaption></figure>
    <figure data-topic="saving goals challenge"><div class="graphic steps-graphic"><i>Start</i><i>Track</i><i>Repeat</i><i>Goal</i></div><figcaption><b>The saving loop</b><span>Consistency matters more than a perfect start.</span></figcaption></figure>
    <figure data-topic="needs wants decision"><div class="graphic compare-graphic"><span>NEED<small>Required now</small></span><b>or</b><span>WANT<small>Can wait</small></span></div><figcaption><b>The pause test</b><span>A quick decision guide for purchases.</span></figcaption></figure>
    <figure data-topic="budget monthly cycle plan review"><div class="graphic cycle-graphic"><span>1<small>Plan</small></span><b>→</b><span>2<small>Spend</small></span><b>→</b><span>3<small>Review</small></span></div><figcaption><b>The monthly budget cycle</b><span>Plan, spend mindfully, review, and improve.</span></figcaption></figure>
</div><p id="no-results" class="no-results" hidden>No matching learning content was found. Try a broader word.</p></div></section>

<section class="section assistant-section" id="assistant"><div class="container assistant-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">BudgetBee assistant</span><h2>Ask a basic money question</h2><p>Get a quick, beginner-friendly BudgetBasics answer about everyday money planning.</p><div class="prompt-list"><button type="button">What is a need?</button><button type="button">How much should I save?</button><button type="button">How do I avoid overspending?</button><button type="button">How do I start an emergency fund?</button></div><small>Educational information only—not professional financial advice. Do not enter private financial or bank details.</small></div><div class="chat-card"><div class="chat-head"><span class="bee" aria-hidden="true">B</span><div><b>BudgetBee</b><small>Budgeting education assistant</small></div><i>● Online</i><button id="clear-chat" class="clear-chat" type="button" aria-label="Clear conversation">Clear</button></div><div id="chat-messages" class="chat-messages" role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="false"><div class="bot-message">Hi! Ask me about budgeting, saving, expenses, needs and wants, debt basics, or spending habits.</div></div><form id="chat-form" autocomplete="off"><label class="visually-hidden" for="chat-question">Your question</label><input id="chat-question" name="Question" maxlength="300" placeholder="Type your question…" aria-describedby="chat-help" required /><button type="submit" aria-label="Ask BudgetBee">→</button></form><small id="chat-help" class="chat-help">Maximum 300 characters. BudgetBasics does not permanently store your questions.</small></div></div></section>

<section class="section section-tint" id="contact"><div class="container contact-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">About BudgetBasics</span><h2>Built for students, not bankers.</h2><p>BudgetBasics turns essential personal-finance ideas into friendly explanations and safe practice tools. It never performs real transactions or asks for bank details.</p><div class="contact-points"><span>Created by the BudgetBasics Student Development Team</span><a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact">Contact and social sharing options →</a></div></div><form id="feedback-form" class="feedback-card" novalidate><h3>Share feedback</h3><div class="form-pair"><label>Name<input name="Name" autocomplete="name" required minlength="2" maxlength="80" /></label><label>Email<input name="Email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254" /></label></div><label>Rating<select name="Rating" required><option value="">Choose</option><option value="5">5 - Excellent</option><option value="4">4 - Good</option><option value="3">3 - Okay</option><option value="2">2 - Needs work</option><option value="1">1 - Poor</option></select></label><label>Comments<textarea name="Comments" required minlength="5" maxlength="500" rows="4"></textarea></label><button class="btn btn-dark" type="submit">Submit feedback</button><p id="feedback-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><small>Your feedback is stored securely in SQL Server. Never include bank or card details.</small></form></div></section>
